<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 22.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to March 22.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to March 22 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week March 16-March 22</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,816,596 tns	204,543 tns    11.26 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,935,010 tns	220,665 tns    11.40 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,825,667 tns	206,350 tns    11.30 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to March 22</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97    25,687,664 tns    2,759,230 tns    10.74 pct</p>
<p>     95-96    25,032,289 tns    2,656,210 tns    10.61 pct</p>
<p>     94-95    23,759,758 tns    2,494,039 tns    10.50 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 59 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 60 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 60 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9530))</p>
